findings.body:
`handleShowReaderModeAction` used to set `displayView: .readerMode`, which the BVC switch maps to `toggleReaderMode()`. This PR changes it to `.readerModeLongPressAction`, which maps to `toggleReaderModeLongPressAction()`, and that function creates a Reading List record for the current URL.

The accessibility magic tap in `BrowserViewController.accessibilityPerformMagicTap` dispatches `GeneralBrowserActionType.showReaderMode`. After this change, VoiceOver users who use the magic tap to toggle reader mode will instead add the page to their Reading List. The `.readerMode` case in `handleDisplayActions` is now unreachable.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/BrowserViewController/State/BrowserViewControllerState.swift" lines="559-570"}

::callout{type="warning"}
Nothing in the QR removal requires this mapping change. Restore `.readerMode` here unless the Reading List behavior is intended, and add a test for the `showReaderMode` display state.

::suggestion{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/BrowserViewController/State/BrowserViewControllerState.swift" lines="566-566"}
            displayView: .readerMode,

In `recordReaderModeTelemetry`, the `isReaderModeEnabled` switch was flipped. The inline comment says the button "will be enabled after action gets executed" when the state is `.available`, so `.available` should give `true`. The PR now gives `false` for `.available` and `true` for every other state. Reader-mode tap analytics will report the wrong enabled value.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Toolbars/Redux/ToolbarMiddleware.swift" lines="521-528"}

This change has nothing to do with QR removal. There is also no test for `readerModeButtonTapped`'s `isEnabled` argument, so the inversion went unnoticed.

::suggestion{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Toolbars/Redux/ToolbarMiddleware.swift" lines="524-525"}
        case .available: true // will be enabled after action gets executed
        default: false

`cancelEditMode` used to keep the selected tab's URL only when it was a web page and not a reader-mode URL. The PR changes that to keep the URL when it is a web page or a reader-mode URL. That changes what the address bar shows after cancelling edit mode. It is also unrelated to QR removal, and no test covers the reader-mode branch.

::diff{file="firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Toolbars/Redux/ToolbarMiddleware.swift" lines="482-491"}

If the flip is intentional, it needs its own PR and a test. If it was an accidental edit, revert it.
